<h3>Who books a move-in clean in Hull</h3>
<p>Hull is one of the more affordable cities in England to buy a home, and many of our move-in cleans are for first-time buyers taking on a terraced house around Newington, Southcoates or the streets off Anlaby Road. Others are families moving up to a bigger semi in west Hull or Sutton-on-Hull, or into a newer house in Kingswood. We also clean for people relocating to Hull for work at the port, in offshore wind, at Hull Royal Infirmary or at the University of Hull, who are often arranging the move from a distance. Tenants moving into rented flats in the city centre or around the Marina book us too, especially when the place has stood empty for a while.</p>
<h3>What we find in Hull homes</h3>
<p>Hard water is the first thing most newcomers notice. Previous owners rarely descale before they go, so we often find thick limescale on shower heads, taps, toilets and sinks. Older terraced houses can have black mould spots on window reveals and bathroom ceilings where condensation has gathered; we clean surface mould and point out anywhere it keeps coming back, as that usually needs a ventilation fix. Fridges and freezers left switched off with the door shut are another regular find, and cooker hoods are often clogged with the last occupant’s grease. The inside of the oven usually needs attention too, so it’s worth adding an <a href="/services/oven-cleaning/">oven clean</a> when you book. Our <a href="/guides/move-in-cleaning-checklist/">move-in cleaning checklist</a> lists everything worth checking in a new home.</p>
<h3>Getting the timing right</h3>
<p>On completion day, keys are usually released only once the money has gone through, which can be any time from late morning onwards. If you can, book your clean for completion afternoon and your removals for the next morning; even half a day of empty rooms makes a big difference. Hull’s terraced streets often have nowhere for a van to stop outside, so having the house clean before boxes start stacking up in a narrow hallway saves a lot of shuffling. We can collect keys from your estate agent or letting agent and return them afterwards, and our <a href="/guides/moving-house-cleaning-timeline/">moving house cleaning timeline</a> helps you plan the weeks either side.</p>
